### Visits: a technician's booked slot on a job. Three constructs, each with its control:
###   - an exclusion `["technician_id"]` over `[starts_at, ends_at)`: one technician, one place at a time
###   - a lookup check: no visit on a completed or cancelled job, with the author's message
###   - a rollup: the job's `on_site_minutes` is the sum of its visits' `minutes_on_site`
### The rows created here are what 150-Relations reads.

### A scheduled job assigned to tech-north
# @name CreateJob3401
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "reference": "WO-3401", "title": "Visits: WO-3401", "status": "scheduled", "priority": 3, "access_code": "ACME-3401", "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}", "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}", "assigned_to": "{{userTechNorth}}", "scheduled_for": "2026-12-01T10:00:00+00:00" }

### A scheduled job assigned to NOBODY — 150-Relations needs a visit whose job no technician holds
# @name CreateJob3402
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "reference": "WO-3402", "title": "Visits: WO-3402", "status": "scheduled", "priority": 3, "access_code": "ACME-3402", "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}", "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}", "scheduled_for": "2026-12-01T10:00:00+00:00" }

### A job already signed off (a create is no transition, so it can be imported completed)
# @name CreateJob3403
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "reference": "WO-3403", "title": "Visits: WO-3403", "status": "completed", "priority": 3, "access_code": "ACME-3403", "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}", "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}", "completed_on": "2026-11-30" }

### tech-north, 10:00-11:00, 45 minutes on site
# @name V1
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "work_order_id": "{{CreateJob3401.response.body.$.id}}", "technician_id": "{{userTechNorth}}", "starts_at": "2026-12-01T10:00:00+00:00", "ends_at": "2026-12-01T11:00:00+00:00", "minutes_on_site": 45 }

### tech-north again, 10:30-11:30: overlaps V1
# @name Overlap
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [409]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "work_order_id": "{{CreateJob3401.response.body.$.id}}", "technician_id": "{{userTechNorth}}", "starts_at": "2026-12-01T10:30:00+00:00", "ends_at": "2026-12-01T11:30:00+00:00" }

### tech-north, 11:00-12:00: starts exactly where V1 ends — `[from, to)`, so no overlap (control)
# @name BackToBack
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "work_order_id": "{{CreateJob3401.response.body.$.id}}", "technician_id": "{{userTechNorth}}", "starts_at": "2026-12-01T11:00:00+00:00", "ends_at": "2026-12-01T12:00:00+00:00", "minutes_on_site": 30 }

### spare-north at V1's exact slot, on the unassigned job: the exclusion is per technician (control)
# @name OtherTechSameSlot
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "work_order_id": "{{CreateJob3402.response.body.$.id}}", "technician_id": "{{userSpareNorth}}", "starts_at": "2026-12-01T10:00:00+00:00", "ends_at": "2026-12-01T11:00:00+00:00" }

